# Timbre — environment
#
# Two variables. Timbre stores nothing about anyone: playlists, profile and
# history live in the reader's browser, so there is no database, no session
# secret and no mail server to configure.

# The YouTube Music sidecar. Loopback in development; never expose it publicly.
YTMUSIC_SERVICE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# Shared with the sidecar so nothing else can call it.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
YTMUSIC_SHARED_SECRET=

# Optional, and unset by default. SoundCloud's *player* needs no credentials at
# all — only its catalogue search does, and that is gated. See docs/BLOCKED.md.
# SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_ID=
# SOUNDCLOUD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Self-hosters only, and unset in the hosted build on purpose. Points at an
# api-v2-shaped base *you* run, which makes SoundCloud's catalogue searchable —
# a soundcloak instance exposes one, with EnableAPI turned on:
#   SOUNDCLOUD_API_BASE=https://your-instance.example/_/api/v2
# Setting it moves the technique, the IP and the terms exposure to you. Leave it
# unset and SoundCloud still plays a pasted URL, exactly as before.

# The same escape hatch for operators with nowhere to run an instance — Timbre
# resolves a guest client_id from soundcloud.com itself and calls api-v2 directly.
# No second service, which is the only way this works on a free serverless host.
# Identical bargain: unset here and in the hosted build, and turning it on moves
# the technique, the IP and the terms exposure to you. See docs/BLOCKED.md.
# SOUNDCLOUD_DIRECT_API=true
